// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'SnowflakeUDFDeploymentConfiguration'. Valid alternatives: ['SnowflakeApp', 'SnowflakeAppDeploymentConfiguration', 'SnowflakeM2MUdf']
//
// `SnowflakeUDFDeploymentConfiguration` used as an element keyword. The token is declared by
// SnowflakeLexerGrammar and it is NOT dead -- it appears in the `identifier` alternation, so
// it is a perfectly good name for something -- but no element rule produces it:
// SnowflakeParserGrammar.g4:87 lists only SNOWFLAKE_APP__CONFIGURATION as a deployment config.
//
// So the grammar declares the deployment configuration of the M2M UDF activator and provides
// no way to write one. The only reachable spelling is as a NAME, which is what the last
// element of ../fixtures/t2-snowflake.pure does.
//
// A rewrite that builds its element table from the token list -- a natural thing to do when
// three of the four vocabulary entries ARE elements -- gains a fourth element kind that
// upstream cannot parse and no protocol class consumes. The alternative list in the message
// is the authoritative set.
###Snowflake
SnowflakeUDFDeploymentConfiguration fixture::neg::UdfConfig
{
   activationConnection : fixture::neg::Conn;
}
